# Line-ending form is pinned to LF for the kit's own hook/tool scripts
# and git-hook shell scripts, plus the two boot files this port's own
# tools/session_context.py measures BY ON-DISK BYTE SIZE (stat().st_size):
# BOOT BUDGET (boot_budget_lines()), the personal CLAUDE.md WARN
# threshold (CLAUDE_WARN), and the Layer A "on disk" byte figure
# (layer_a_lines()) all read the file's size straight off the
# filesystem -- a checkout that rewrites LF -> CRLF (or the reverse,
# core.autocrlf-dependent) silently changes that size and can move a
# WARN/OVER verdict without any real content change. Same class the
# staff deployment's own .gitattributes exists for (byte-budget
# measured by on-disk form -- docs/SIBLING_MAP.md, axis 14 there).
#
# Scripts: a CRLF shebang line under .githooks/ silently breaks hook
# execution on a Linux clone; a mixed CRLF/LF split was found on disk
# empirically across toolkit/tools/*.py and toolkit/.githooks/* during
# this port (2026-08-25) -- this pin normalizes checkouts going
# forward, it does not itself rewrite any file's current content.
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
BOOT.md text eol=lf
tools/*.py text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
